\title{Three hardware bounds and two times}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786316438936}
\meta{anki-deck}{MLSys}

\prompt{What three hardware quantities bound the runtime of any algorithm, and what are the two time formulas?}{
  Compute (OPs/s), bandwidth (bytes/s), and total memory (bytes). Everything an accelerator can do is rationed by one of the three, and the first two give the only two times worth computing:

  ##{T_{\mathrm{math}} = \frac{\text{computation FLOPs}}{\text{accelerator FLOPs/s}}, \qquad T_{\mathrm{comms}} = \frac{\text{communication bytes}}{\text{bandwidth (bytes/s)}}}

  "Comms" means either HBM #{\leftrightarrow} compute cores within a chip, or chip #{\leftrightarrow} chip over ICI / DCN / PCIe. Same formula either way — only the bandwidth in the denominator changes, which is why the same model covers a [[NZZ7]] memory stall and a [[A7PN]] all-reduce.
}
